=Write the body of a short reply email to an inbound commercial solar enquiry.

Their name: {{ $('Score And Tier Lead').item.json.name }}
Their company: {{ $('Score And Tier Lead').item.json.company }}
Property type: {{ $('Score And Tier Lead').item.json.propertyType }}
Stated consumption: {{ $('Score And Tier Lead').item.json.monthlyKwh }} kWh per month
Roof: {{ $('Score And Tier Lead').item.json.roofType }}
The problem they described: {{ $('Score And Tier Lead').item.json.painPoint }}
Their original message: {{ $('Score And Tier Lead').item.json.message }}
Who will follow up: {{ $('Assign Rep').item.json.repName }}

Rules: acknowledge the specific problem they described in their own terms. Do NOT quote a price, a payback period, a system size, a tariff or a saving figure - none of those can be known before a site assessment, and stating one creates a commitment we cannot honour. Do not invent incentives, grants or tax credits. Say only that the rep will be in touch to arrange a site assessment. Four sentences maximum. Plain text, no subject line, no greeting and no sign-off - those are added separately.

